<title>GERMANY: Merrill gets mandate for Hoechst US listing.</title>
<headline>Merrill gets mandate for Hoechst US listing.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals company Hoechst AG said on Monday that Merrill Lynch will handle its listing of shares on the New York Stock Exchange in October.</p>
<p>Bank of New York will be the custody bank for Hoechst's American Depositary Receipts (ADRs), a Hoechst spokesman said in response to a Reuter enquiry.</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch will be Hoechst's consultant in the listing and will also organise presentations to investors.</p>
<p>Hoechst has already said it does not plan a capital increase in conjunction with the listing.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
